<UL TYPE=SQUARE><LI>Time/Day is pretty important.  2-3 hrs 1 time per week just isn't enough time.  Knowing that 1/2 the group would be on EST ( Foggy, Doxx, Foggy's friends )..starting at 7-8pm CST would just be too late for them on a weeknight.  I'd look into a weekend instead, maybe every other weekend or something similiar.  Having 4-8 hrs to play is MUCH better!  Weekends can be a bit harder to consistantly schedule though.<BR><LI>Classes - You need (1) Cleric and an (2) Enchanter.  You need a (3) Tank. Tank can be a warrior ( preferrable ), SK or Paladin.  You need a (4)Porter ( Wizard or Druid ) and you need a (5)SoW person ( Druid or Shaman ).  That leaves one spot that can be anything.  If you go with a Druid as your porter, then you take care of the SoW part too leaving you with 2 optional slots to fill.  Rogues are damn nice for damage output, while Monks are damn nice for FD Pulling.  Mages are great due to nukes, pet dmg output and summons.  Forgot to buy food/water before starting?  No worries.  Need 100% weight reduction loot bags for all the Fine Steel...got that covered too.  Necros are also darn nice to have in a group.<BR><LI>People Factor - Real life or just people with different levels of dedication to EQ should also be taken into account.  Remember the last Bravo group and how it stopped playing.  If you can't have a full group...go with a partial group or even a duo.  Having just one other person that you can consistantly group and level with is TONS better then solo.<BR></UL><P><B>Good full group wish list</B><BR><OL TYPE=1><BR><LI>Cleric*<BR><LI>Enchanter*<BR><LI>Warrior* or SK/Paladin<BR><LI>Druid <I>Alt: Wizard</I><BR><LI>Rogue <I>Alt: Shaman</I><BR><LI>Magician or Necro <I>Alt: Monk/Rogue/Bard</I><BR></OL><BR>*=Key people who should be the most experienced players<P>I'd suggest setting a meeting time where you all create lvl one gnome newbies. That will 1) Allow you all to chat about it in real time and face to face and 2) Give you a good idea for who is really interested and willing to put for the effort into making the group work.<P>We can have Ghall or Nefarius make a /guildmotd to advertise the meeting for the people that may not hit the boards that often or at all.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song<BR>Sleethr - 54th DE Mage<BR>Medec - 41st level Battle Cleric<BR>Meekka - 33rd DE Rogue<BR>Vowk - 27th Dr00d
